+<script type="application/ld+json">{"@context":"https://schema.org","@type":"FAQPage","mainEntity":[{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Garden City, SC in Horry County or Georgetown County?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Both. The county line crosses the beach about a third of a mile south of the Garden City Pier. The pier is in Horry County, and about 3.2 of the beach road's 5 miles are in Georgetown County."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Garden City part of Myrtle Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"No. Garden City has no town government of its own and is not part of any city. Most addresses use Murrells Inlet, ZIP code 29576."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Can you drive a golf cart on Garden City Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"On the Horry County beach, from November 1 to February 28, with a state permit and a licensed driver."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Are dogs allowed on Garden City Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Not from 10 a.m. to 5 p.m., May 1 through Labor Day, on the Horry County beach. At other times, on a hand-held leash no longer than 7 feet."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Garden City, SC safe?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"We do not rate any place as safe or unsafe. Garden City has no town police department, because it has no town government."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What schools serve Garden City, SC?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Schools are assigned by address, by the school district of the county the home is in. We look up the assigned schools for any home you like."}}]}</script>
