th, and the top tenth $10,700 or more. For one home, enter its address and bedroom count in the Airbnb income calculator: it compares the home with similar listings nearby."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the average Airbnb occupancy rate in Garden City Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Listings in Garden City Beach were booked on 40% of available nights over the past year. That compares with 39% for the South Carolina average. July is usually the busiest month."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much does an Airbnb cost per night in Garden City Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The average booked night in Garden City Beach cost $371 before fees. Half of listings charge between $205 and $420, so bedroom count and location move the price more than the average suggests."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Do you need a permit for an Airbnb in Garden City Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"None of the active Garden City Beach listings display a registration, permit or license number. That doesn't mean no rules apply, so confirm registration, permit and occupancy-tax rules with the city or county before buying."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"Is Airbnb profitable in Garden City Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Yes, when it's run well. The average Garden City Beach Airbnb grossed $41,223 in the 12 months to September 2026, 10% above the South Carolina average of $37,525. Run by its owner, with the cleaning fee covering the cleaner and everyday costs for Airbnb's fee, utilities, supplies, upkeep and insurance, $25,333 a year (about $2,110 a month) is left before the mortgage or rent. A home that costs less than that to own or rent makes a profit, and a listing at the top-quarter mark leaves about $3,610 a month. Check a specific home in the Airbnb calculator."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"When is Airbnb peak season in Garden City Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"July usually pays best, averaging $10,200 per active listing over the past two years, and January usually pays least. The month-by-month table above shows how the latest 12 months played out."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What is the Airbnb RevPAR in Garden City Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Each night a Garden City Beach listing was open to book earned $159 on average over the past year, booked or not. That figure, revenue per available night (RevPAR), folds price and occupancy into one number; the top 10% of listings made $331 or more."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How far in advance do guests book Airbnbs in Garden City Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Garden City Beach stays were booked 73 days (about two and a half months) before arrival on average over the past year, so a listing that opens its calendar late misses many bookings."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How long do guests stay at Airbnbs in Garden City Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"The average Garden City Beach Airbnb stay lasted 5.1 nights over the past year. A listing took 21 reservations over the year on average."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How are Airbnbs in Garden City Beach rated?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Guests rate Garden City Beach Airbnbs 4.80 out of 5 on average. Guests score location highest and cleanliness lowest."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"What are the best neighborhoods for Airbnb in Garden City Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"Garden City Beach and Georgetown draw the most short-term rental interest in Garden City Beach. The neighborhood guide explains what brings guests to each."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How many Airbnbs are there in Garden City Beach?","acceptedAnswer":{"@type":"Answer","text":"AirROI counted 374 active Airbnb listings in Garden City Beach as of September 2026. The closest tracked market is Murrells Inlet, 3 km away."}},{"@type":"Question","name":"How much are Airbnb cleaning fees i